{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/528342-the-fae-touched","id":528342,"title":"The Fae-Touched","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-05-25T18:32:20-07:00","id":528342,"title":"The Fae-Touched","content":"Discuss here. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/changeling-the-lost-second-edition-the-fae-touched/\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://theonyxpath.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/11/OPP-Metal.png\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/changeling-the-lost-second-edition-the-fae-touched/\" target=\"_blank\"> Changeling the Lost: Second Edition, The Fae-Touched &ndash; Onyx Path Publishing </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/changeling-the-lost-second-edition-the-fae-touched/\" target=\"_blank\"> http://theonyxpath.com/changeling-the-lost-second-edition-the-fae-touched/ </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-25T18:36:12-07:00","id":528361,"title":"","content":"Oh man, I love these guys!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-25T18:57:39-07:00","id":528373,"title":"","content":"I love this sooooooo much! Some of my favorite changeling stories focused on a human searching for their taken loved one. Sarah from Labyrinth, Poison from Poison, arguably Virginia and Tony from 10th Kindom, Christine Colins from Changeling (yeah, yeah, that one doesn't actually involve fae, but still...) I'm so happy to see such characters are going to be the new Changeling minor template!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-25T20:01:47-07:00","id":528423,"title":"","content":"you know, the blog doesnt appear in the main page. It goes from dark age mage to monday meeting","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1351-sakii","name":"Sakii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1351_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-25T20:04:12-07:00","id":528425,"title":"","content":"It was there before, I swear.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-25T20:24:06-07:00","id":528445,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/528342-the-fae-touched?p=528425#post528425\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It was there before, I swear.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I originally linked to the blog post from the OPP Twitter feed. However, it does not seem to appear if you simply go to the OPP homepage.<br /> <br /> David has somehow offended the internet gods. Woe be to David. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-25T20:45:02-07:00","id":528456,"title":"","content":"Yeah, weird, it just... does not seem to be there, now. :/ Maybe they wanted to keep the Monday Meeting Update on top for a bit longer, and so pulled the Fae-Touched teaser for a bit to make that so...?<br /> <br /> Either way, if Charlaquin's post is anything to go by, I'm really going to be looking forward to this one. ^_^<br /> <br /> EDIT: Op, definitely back up now! And indeed, I am digging this happy serving of awesome. ^__^ Alas, it's 17 pages and I have a busy day ahead tomorrow. Gonna have to put off the rest until later.<br /> <br /> EDIT2: And, uh, it disappeared again. o_o Wut. Eh, odds are pretty good it'll be back soon enough, and it matters less with the link Arc helpfully provided.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":558,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","user":"Gaius","date":"05-26-2015, 12:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-25T20:51:17-07:00","id":528460,"title":"","content":"It's really funny reading this with the terminology of 1E Changeling in my head. I got to the bit where they have Seemings and had a moment of &quot;They're 2E's Kithless?&quot;<br /> <br /> Which, yeah, obviously they are. It just has clearly different connotations in 2E.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-25T20:59:34-07:00","id":528463,"title":"","content":"I really like these guys. Let me see if I can dig them out of my history....<br /> <br /> EDIT: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1ChFsnFToDqIWjTXSFt7jjPtMQfvXE8TdTmenL3Thj98/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Here ya go people.</a> Remember that I love you all, but not as much as the writers of Changeling do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 05-26-2015, 12:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-25T20:59:44-07:00","id":528464,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gaius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/528342-the-fae-touched?p=528456#post528456\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, weird, it just... does not seem to be there, now. :/ Maybe they wanted to keep the Monday Meeting Update on top for a bit longer, and so pulled the Fae-Touched teaser for a bit to make that so...?<br /> <br /> Either way, if Charlaquin's post is anything to go by, I'm really going to be looking forward to this one. ^_^</div> </div> </div> </div>I think maybe so. I forget sometimes, that what's Tuesday for me, is Monday for the rest of the team.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-25T21:02:05-07:00","id":528468,"title":"","content":"holy fuck these guys are awesome.<br /> <br /> my shift key shorted out from the sheer fanboy glee i am feeling.<br /> <br /> holy fuck.<br /> <br /> <br /> More seriously, I assume fae-touched whose friends manage to come back the same time as they do remain as such, but don't have as much of an obsession with the Hedge?<br /> <br /> Cause I'm writing a Changeling crossover fanfic right now, and the &quot;bad ending&quot; (I'm going to write two) involves the protagonists being taken by the Fae...and the one left behind ends up becoming fae-touched by simply taking up on a promise he made to handle the consequences if he was wrong. Closing lines are his reunion with them on Earth.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Ah, didn't read the whole thing. They're pretty hedgebound.<br /> <br /> Though, is there any way to <i>maybe </i>increase a Touched's life expectancy somewhat? Seems that would be a worthy plot hook. Also, what happens to an already older person who gets Touched?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":180,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","user":"Leliel","date":". 05-26-2015, 12:22 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-25T21:41:01-07:00","id":528515,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/528342-the-fae-touched?p=528468#post528468\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Though, is there any way to <i>maybe </i>increase a Touched's life expectancy somewhat? Seems that would be a worthy plot hook. Also, what happens to an already older person who gets Touched?</div> </div> </div> </div>Hm. Don't see why not. And, not sure. Gonna give it some thought.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-25T22:05:10-07:00","id":528537,"title":"","content":"I see the link between fae-touched entry and changeling egress and a pair of words occur to me that will hopefully make sense to other people:<br /> <br /> &quot;Circumstantial simultaneity.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-25T23:02:46-07:00","id":528569,"title":"","content":"So I noticed Fae-Touched have a Seeming and all its associated benefits (and drawbacks) but they do not have Clarity. I assume that means their Blessing increases their Integrity and their Curse is an Integrity Breaking Point, but the text doesn't specify that and it probably should.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-25T23:08:33-07:00","id":528572,"title":"","content":"I feel foolish for having missed that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-25T23:17:30-07:00","id":528577,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/528342-the-fae-touched?p=528569#post528569\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I noticed Fae-Touched have a Seeming and all its associated benefits (and drawbacks) but they do not have Clarity. I assume that means their Blessing increases their Integrity and their Curse is an Integrity Breaking Point, but the text doesn't specify that and it probably should.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's because it was written before we settled on Seeming Blessings and Curses. I'll note it. I'm pretty sure I'm going with Integrity as the analogue, as noted.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-26T05:49:50-07:00","id":528731,"title":"","content":"On page 6 now of preview, but I have some questions to the text and rules of Fae-Touched.<br /> <br /> 1. When <b><i>exactly</i></b> mortal character acquire Fae-Touched Template? When they first time enter Hedge? When they leave the Hedge? Or do they need to meet the changeling character that summoned character into it?<br /> <br /> 2. Could Fae-Touched status be heredity in some situations? Like assume that modern characters grandfather become Fae-Touched as he was looking for his wife abducted years ago. He could not find her, even if he did not stop to look for his first, true love. His promise was not broken, yet he did not found his love. Promise for finding grandmother, now changeling, goes to the granddaughter that is marked from the birth or maybe just after she hears a story about grandmother - and she becomes Fae Touched when she starts to look for her in Hedge, &quot;inheriting&quot; the grandfathers promise.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 05-26-2015, 09:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-26T06:28:54-07:00","id":528746,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/528342-the-fae-touched?p=528731#post528731\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1. When <b><i>exactly</i></b> mortal character acquire Fae-Touched Template? When they first time enter Hedge? When they leave the Hedge? Or do they need to meet the changeling character that summoned character into it?</div> </div> </div> </div>You missed it:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Becoming Fae-Touched (p. 2)</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Once in the Hedge, the fate of the person is sealed. She is now fae-touched despite what else happens.</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 2. Could Fae-Touched status be heredity in some situations? Like assume that modern characters grandfather become Fae-Touched as he was looking for his wife abducted years ago. He could not find her, even if he did not stop to look for his first, true love. His promise was not broken, yet he did not found his love. Promise for finding grandmother, now changeling, goes to the granddaughter that is from the birth or maybe just after she hears a story about grandmother - she becomes Fae Touched when she starts to look for her, &quot;inheriting&quot; the grandfathers promise. </div> </div> </div>That's actually an interesting idea. Not Dave, obviously, but I imagine it wouldn't happen by default (possibly unless the original promise was a bit more... explicitly familial than most would be), and wouldn't be at all common regardless; that the fae-touched character originally forged a personal connection with the Changeling feels important to me, and that's something a descendant is unlikely to have. Still, some potentially interesting stories, there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-26T06:31:28-07:00","id":528750,"title":"","content":"So Hedge Addiction calls for a Willpower roll; I've only seen that in OWoD, so I wonder if that's meant to be a Resolve + Composure roll.<br /> <br /> And I'll have to see how much of the new dreaming rules I can suss out of the Merits...<br /> <br /> Too Solid Flesh? I wonder what that does...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-26T10:29:53-07:00","id":528923,"title":"","content":"I like the Fae-Touched. I like them <i>a lot</i>.<br /> <br /> There's so much potential in their writing and the essence of their connection to faerie. That their promise to a Changeling carries within their soul a piece of the Wyrd the moment they step into the Hedge, enacting it as something concrete.<br /> <br /> Much fun to be had with them. And also &quot;oh why my heart why&quot; levels of heartbreaking.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-26T10:42:15-07:00","id":528953,"title":"","content":"So overall I like it.<br /> <br /> My primary concern might sound a little odd, but I felt it was a little too easy to become Fae Touched. What I mean by that is that I can't see any way for; E.G. a mother to try and rescue her stolen child without becoming Fae-Tocuhed.<br /> <br /> I suppose it comes down to a the exact definition of a promise - but I would imagine that mothers who promise to always be there for their children is the default state of motherhood. This means that it's actually hard to have regular mortals dedicated to rescuing Changelings without them becoming Fae-Touched.<br /> <br /> I suppose the answer could be &quot;is the game you're playing called Hunter or Changeling?&quot; but I do think that a mortal trying to rescue a Changeling would make a good Lost NPC because Changelings would relate to the differently than to Fae Touched. It would also support the thematic point that mortals are awesome - and it was a bad thing that a Changeling's mortalness was stolen. <hr /><br /> Now for various smaller points:<br /> <br /> Is there enough spare wordcount for a Promise of Vengeance merit? Now he's the beloved Spring King, but once upon a time he was the junkie who knifed your son and you haven't forgiven him.<br /> <br /> A possible effect would be that the Wyrd knows <i>it's personal</i>. Other people tend to stay out of your conflicts. If you can explain why someone's wronged you, or you have a sealed oath to avenge a wrong on someone else's behalf then any attempt to talk yourself out of trouble requires two fewer doors. If that Spring King does the sensible thing and tells the police he has a stalker, reduce the Doors by two to convince them to stay out of it. In addition you've got bonus dice on Integrity Breaking Points in pursuit of vengeance. <hr /><br /> One thing I wasn't clear on is what percentage of Fae Touched have completed their quest to rescue someone? The impression I got is that most Fae Touched upon entering the Hedge end up dead or enslaved, with only a small minority returning to Earth without completing their quest and different small minority returning victorious. After all, upon entering the Hedge they have a direct line to their Changeling.<br /> <br /> I just wanted to check if that's true? <hr /><br /> The Drawbacks didn't feel right to me. Shortened lifespan is fine, though mostly a non-issue since games typically don't last that long. However the other three didn't feel right.<br /> <br /> Arcadian Dreams: A good concept but dicepool penalties are a bit bland. Perhaps something like the Spooked Condition which explicitly encourages the player to go chasing the missing Changeling. Memories of their dreams give them fresh clues or red herrings to peruse. Alternatively give them a new Condition that's identical to Spooked, except it gives you -2 to all unrelated actions unless you spend a Willpower to suppress it for a scene. The bit about sensing the direction to their Changeling in the Hedge should probably be moved from Drawbacks to the powers section.<br /> <br /> Hedge Addiction: As written this will just get worse and worse over time until you're at -5 penalties. Some way to reset the counter is required. More to the point, I couldn't find anything on what they actually do in the Hedge. Do they just have a picnic near the gate then go home? I feel that the core Fae-Tocuhed concept doesn't have enough ties to the Hedge in of itself to provide answers. I imagine they're probably not mounting a rescue attempt because that's mostly a succeed or die thing. Key Smiths make it seem like a long term lifestyle.<br /> <br /> Susceptible to Madness - I understand the logic but the Madness Condition is just penalties to random dicepools. Crucially it didn't help either players or Storytellers portray madness. I wasn't too fond of it in GMC and I think it has the same problem here. Advising the storyteller to inflict Conditions penalties on Breaking Point failures or writing a new more focused Condition (perhaps one of the ones for Changelings will be suitable) could fix it. <hr /><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">When this happens, her only hope is that a changeling comes across her, as eventually her presence is noticed by one Gentry or another and she is taken. </span></span></span> </div> </div> </div> There's probably some cool plot hooks that could happen if you say turning into a hobgoblin is another possibility. <hr /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/528342-the-fae-touched?p=528515#post528515\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hm. Don't see why not. And, not sure. Gonna give it some thought.</div> </div> </div> </div>Buying lifespan from a Goblin Market is the obvious solution - even if they burn through brought years as fast as their natural ones you can still split the payments over years.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-26T11:03:26-07:00","id":528982,"title":"","content":"The other way of fixing a fae touched lifespan is to make a deal with the Gentry and become a changeling (a fixed-term contract perhaps?).<br /> <br /> Many solutions, each more horrific than the last.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-26T11:42:26-07:00","id":529056,"title":"","content":"I assume that when a fae -touched has extremely expressive, the changeling gains two glamour for every glamour the fae-touched loses?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-26T14:54:45-07:00","id":529300,"title":"","content":"I really like the basic premise here. Though, the implications of how they can become one and how rare it is to get back afterward tell me there would be far fewer fae touched than other half splats, and that they're likely around the same number, if not fewer, of changelings themselves. That always feels a little off for a half splat, in my opinion, but maybe that's just me.<br /> <br /> I'm also not a big fan of the shortened lifespan. It comes across to me as a &quot;Why?&quot; type of thing; the explanation is kinda meh, and it doesn't really do anything to make me think &quot;Yep, that's a hedge-connected mortal thing right there&quot; at all.<br /> <br /> That said, I do love how much more they can do now, even if some of those mechanics clearly need to be spoiled to us in other blogs. It makes them feel actually supernatural instead of just being superfluous like in 1e. The merits are also very flavorful and thematic, I'm definitely a fan of the way they build on the template and the fluff behind it.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-26T15:04:06-07:00","id":529304,"title":"","content":"First edition fae touched couldn't have been more crowbarred in if they'd tried, so a step-up was pretty much inevitable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-26T15:25:58-07:00","id":529317,"title":"","content":"I love it so much I want to marry it and take it on an expensive honeymoon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/209-that-other-guy","name":"That Other Guy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-26T16:23:23-07:00","id":529387,"title":"","content":"This is awesome! Not only that, but the references to Oneiromancy and Pledgecraft (or whatever it's called now) are very interesting. It's only a hint, but I like the glimpse I'm getting. Can't wait to see more on those two systems!<br /> <br /> Couple questions:<br /> Is the Wyrd 0 permanent, or can it be raised?<br /> <br /> Similarly, are they limited to 1 dot contracts, or is that just at char gen?<br /> <br /> Will they have the option of not taking a Seeming? If so, how would the Fae Mein merit work? Should it just have an additional prereq of &quot;possess a Seeming&quot;?<br /> <br /> The Hedge Delver merit allows the Fae Touched to add Survival to all non-combat rolls in the Hedge. Does that include social rolls, like bargaining at a Goblin Market? Or rolls to activate Contracts? If yes, that's a pretty sweet merit. A Fae Touched with that merit could be a major asset to a Motley that likes to explore the hedge or deal with Goblin Markets!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5910-csschulz","name":"CSSchulz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5910_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-26T16:34:23-07:00","id":529393,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>falco1029</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/528342-the-fae-touched?p=529300#post529300\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I really like the basic premise here. Though, the implications of how they can become one and how rare it is to get back afterward tell me there would be far fewer fae touched than other half splats, and that they're likely around the same number, if not fewer, of changelings themselves. That always feels a little off for a half splat, in my opinion, but maybe that's just me.<br /> <br /> I'm also not a big fan of the shortened lifespan. It comes across to me as a &quot;Why?&quot; type of thing; the explanation is kinda meh, and it doesn't really do anything to make me think &quot;Yep, that's a hedge-connected mortal thing right there&quot; at all.<br /> <br /> That said, I do love how much more they can do now, even if some of those mechanics clearly need to be spoiled to us in other blogs. It makes them feel actually supernatural instead of just being superfluous like in 1e. The merits are also very flavorful and thematic, I'm definitely a fan of the way they build on the template and the fluff behind it.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that, in retrospect, does seem like a little more tragedy than what may be required or warranted.<br /> <br /> It needs to be dropped or turned into a plot hook (hence my longevity-quest suggestion).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-26T18:52:48-07:00","id":529489,"title":"","content":"Okay, first, the Fae-Touched are <i>awesome</i>. And fit perfectly with a C:tL character concept I've been trying to get working for, like, months. I'm going to be referring to first draft a lot over the next few weeks.<br /> <br /> That said, there are a couple things. The way it's currently written makes it seem like most Fae-Touched are lucky if they escape the Hedge. But the talk of their relative numbers on the flipside makes it seem like most *do* escape the Hedge. I'm having a little difficulty reconciling it.<br /> <br /> I am going to second what a couple others here said: The shortened lifespan thing came out of left-field, and seems like an <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">unnecessary</span> addition in order to make life more 'tragic' for a Fae-Touched. I was reading this, nodding my head at the awesomeness, then hit the shortened lifespan and went 'What? Why!?' Given what I know of Changeling, the only reason I could think this could be a thing is that there's some obscure bit of worldbuilding in 2nd Edition that we aren't aware of to help justify it. Otherwise, the 'reason' for it comes off as very thin, and as just said seems like it was tacked on there because someone wanted to add another layer of 'tragedy' to the Fae-Touched.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4917-alisa180","name":"Alisa180","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-26T19:00:12-07:00","id":529495,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alisa180</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/528342-the-fae-touched?p=529489#post529489\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I am going to second what a couple others here said: The shortened lifespan thing came out of left-field, and seems like an <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">unnecessary</span> addition in order to make life more 'tragic' for a Fae-Touched. I was reading this, nodding my head at the awesomeness, then hit the shortened lifespan and went 'What? Why!?' Given what I know of Changeling, the only reason I could think this could be a thing is that there's some obscure bit of worldbuilding in 2nd Edition that we aren't aware of to help justify it. Otherwise, the 'reason' for it comes off as very thin, and as just said seems like it was tacked on there because someone wanted to add another layer of 'tragedy' to the Fae-Touched.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not entirely in disagreement here. I'm gonna give it some thought. But that's probably getting chopped.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-26T19:13:47-07:00","id":529525,"title":"","content":"For what it's worth, as someone who wasn't bothered by the shortened lifespan thing, I also wouldn't be sad to see it go.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-26T19:16:51-07:00","id":529527,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/528342-the-fae-touched?p=529495#post529495\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm not entirely in disagreement here. I'm gonna give it some thought. But that's probably getting chopped.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, good. Because I was just thinking about it more, and realized that the reasoning verges on an internal contradiction. It says \u2018she has not really be adapted to hold and use Glamour the way a changeling has\u2019 and that\u2019s what causes her shortened lifespan. But what about Fae-Touched that escapes and never uses Glamour again? And isn\u2019t part of the point of being Fae-Touch is to...have a character adapted to holding and using Glamour? That they become natural users of it as a matter of course?<br /> <br /> The writing here makes it seem like the \u2018force\u2019 of Glamour use shortens their lifespans, but by all indications they do it almost as naturally as the Lost. If they were using, say, magic rituals or something to access the Wyrd and Glamour, then it would be more understandable.<br /> <br /> Also, there was this line earlier in the write-up, &quot;The Glamour of the place entered her easily and changed her.&quot; Which stands in almost direct contradiction to the idea that 'not being adapted enough to Glamour' is a reason for the Fae-Touched to have shorted life-spans. Because again, the statement it takes a 'toll' on the character implies a certain degree of forcing Glamour through them, but, well, see what I just wrote in this paragraph, and the above. <br /> <br /> The Wyrd has been associated with twisting things, and this is reflected nicely in the Fae-Touched gaining their own Seeming when/if they escape. Wouldn\u2019t this twisting itself be indicative of adaptation? I\u2019m still mentally working out the metaphysics of how the new take on Seemings work, but in general, the Wyrd tends to force something to adapt, rather then allowing someone to fail to do so. I could understand if a Fae-Touched who never found their way out of the Hedge had a shortened lifespan, provided they live/avoid being captured that long. But for one who\u2019s escaped and gained a Seeming, the reasoning is much more iffy, and harder to accept.<br /> <br /> Not having very long to live is a tragedy in of itself. A big one. One that can easily threaten to overwhelm the already-present tragedy of a Fae-Touched whose 'promised changeling' is still trapped in Arcadia, or the Fae-Toucheds' addiction to the Hedge. It gets even more egregious when one notes how, in 1st edition. exposure to the Wryd increased the lifespan of changelings. Fae-Touched could have normal lifespans, but a greatly shortened one through channeling the Wyrd just doesn't match up with what I know and believe about Changeling.<br /> <br /> All of this, of course, is mostly based on what I've read in the blog posts, and what I've read in 1st Ed. Hence why my previous post had the addendum 'Unless there's some obscure bit of worldbuilding in 2nd Ed. That we aren't aware of yet.'If you want a theme of 'Fae<br /> <br /> Phew. Sorry, I kind of went on there. But I\u2019m glad to hear that it\u2019s probably going to be eliminated anyway. You guys have really done a good job otherwise.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4917,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4917-alisa180","user":"Alisa180","date":". 05-26-2015, 11:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4917-alisa180","name":"Alisa180","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-26T21:10:23-07:00","id":529579,"title":"","content":"Other question I have, beside the possible heradity of Fae-Touched status - they all get new Seeming. But only those with Merit get the Mien, and it's weaker one. So how it works now? Character can have a Fairest Fae-Tocuhed that has only elven ears? Beast one with wild eyes? And those without the Mien have Seeming, but they do not show it?<br /> <br /> And when character et the Seeming? She become Fae-Touched when she <b>first time enter the Hedge</b>. But Seeming is get by changelings in 2ED <b>on escape</b>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-26T21:18:41-07:00","id":529581,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/528342-the-fae-touched?p=529579#post529579\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And when character et the Seeming? She become Fae-Touched when she <b>first time enter the Hedge</b>. But Seeming is get by changelings in 2ED <b>on escape</b>.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's decided when the Fae-touched decides to escape the Hedge, and how they figure out how to.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/287-wildfire","name":"Wildfire","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-26T22:02:11-07:00","id":529596,"title":"","content":"I was just re-reading and caught something.<br /> <br /> Allow me to give you guys credit for the subtle, yet beautiful piece of representation in the paragraph that starts like this:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> A woman comes home to find an uncommonly messy house. Her wife is in the kitchen, preparing dinner. </div> </div> </div>Did anyone else notice what I noticed here? It's a relatively small thing, but I still love it.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4917-alisa180","name":"Alisa180","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-26T22:24:12-07:00","id":529602,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alisa180</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/528342-the-fae-touched?p=529596#post529596\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was just re-reading and caught something.<br /> <br /> Allow me to give you guys credit for the subtle, yet beautiful piece of representation in the paragraph that starts like this:<br /> <br /> Did anyone else notice what I noticed here? It's a relatively small thing, but I still love it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I love my writers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-26T22:25:34-07:00","id":529603,"title":"","content":"Pretty cool, but I feel like the write up should talk more about the Touched who manages to link up with their Changeling on their way out. Yes, I get that there's drama inherent in the tug between the Touched on the search and the trapped Fae and such, but it seems like there's a fair amount of drama in the interactions between the Touched and their Changeling once they've escaped together. The Touched kinda knows the Hedge, but can't really understand what being fully in Fae was like, while the Changeling is now with someone who has the ability to go back, but wants... <i>craves</i> more. How does that relationship evolve?<br /> <br /> I feel like a bit more wordcount could be used there. If nothing else, I'd appreciate it if you could make it explicit as to what happens to their bond if/when they both make it back to the real world, hopefully together.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-26T23:02:40-07:00","id":529616,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/528342-the-fae-touched?p=529603#post529603\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Pretty cool, but I feel like the write up should talk more about the Touched who manages to link up with their Changeling on their way out. Yes, I get that there's drama inherent in the tug between the Touched on the search and the trapped Fae and such, but it seems like there's a fair amount of drama in the interactions between the Touched and their Changeling once they've escaped together. The Touched kinda knows the Hedge, but can't really understand what being fully in Fae was like, while the Changeling is now with someone who has the ability to go back, but wants... <i>craves</i> more. How does that relationship evolve?<br /> <br /> I feel like a bit more wordcount could be used there. If nothing else, I'd appreciate it if you could make it explicit as to what happens to their bond if/when they both make it back to the real world, hopefully together.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm going to second this. Especially that last paragraph since my first thought for the aforementioned character concept was that they'd be a rare case where everything 'went well.' Or at least their friend would be out of Faerie by the end of the first story in the Chronicle. I was dissapointed when the write-up didn't describe what happened to things like the Arcadian Dreams drawback after that.<br /> <br /> That's a flaw in the write-up. The concept of a changeling and a Fae-Touched counterpart presents an absolutely fascinating, and very tempting dynamic for a Chronicle. It's written with the assumption that the changeling the Fae-Touched is connected to never escapes, but I doubt I'll be the only one who wants to play an FT whose changeling does/did.<br /> <br /> Not to mention, since Fae-Touched allow their changelings an opportunity to escape, that has the foundations for a fascinating prelude on the changeling's side, with plenty of potential story hooks (like the Pedro example in the write-up). That's another story oppurtunity I know some are going to want to take advantage of.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4917-alisa180","name":"Alisa180","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-26T23:54:01-07:00","id":529645,"title":"","content":"I'm really loving the Fae-Touched. Their inclusion into the Changeling game just gives it that much more of a mythical feel. <br /> <br /> Here's a question though: Does a Fae-Touched's promise require that they take a Promise Merit, or are the Promise Merits just an optional bonus?<br /> <br /> Either way:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/528342-the-fae-touched?p=528953#post528953\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Is there enough spare wordcount for a Promise of Vengeance merit? Now he's the beloved Spring King, but once upon a time he was the junkie who knifed your son and you haven't forgiven him.<br /> <br /> A possible effect would be that the Wyrd knows <i>it's personal</i>. Other people tend to stay out of your conflicts. If you can explain why someone's wronged you, or you have a sealed oath to avenge a wrong on someone else's behalf then any attempt to talk yourself out of trouble requires two fewer doors. If that Spring King does the sensible thing and tells the police he has a stalker, reduce the Doors by two to convince them to stay out of it. In addition you've got bonus dice on Integrity Breaking Points in pursuit of vengeance. <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>That would be an awesome promise to add!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5700-nuwisha-nutjob","name":"Nuwisha Nutjob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5700_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-27T00:37:51-07:00","id":529668,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alisa180</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/528342-the-fae-touched?p=529596#post529596\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Allow me to give you guys credit for the subtle, yet beautiful piece of representation in the paragraph that starts like this:<br /> <br /> (...)<br /> <br /> Did anyone else notice what I noticed here? It's a relatively small thing, but I still love it.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's second best representation of LGBT characters in 2ED corebooks. First is still in <b>Werewolf: The Forsaken </b>Touchstones section, where male cop character truly loves his boyfriend and want's to be his husband, but understand that him being Uratha would put his loved one in to danger if they would be &quot;serious&quot;. We have gay and lesbian relationships - now I wait for transgender people in <b>Mage </b>2ED. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> On my part, I want to re-ask the question about Seemings of Fae-Touched without Mien they by default do not have.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/528342-the-fae-touched?p=529579#post529579\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Other question I have, beside the possible heredity of Fae-Touched status - they all get new Seeming. But only those with Merit get the Mien, and it's weaker one. So how it works now? Character can have a Fairest Fae-Touched that has only elven ears? Beast one with wild eyes? And those without the Mien have Seeming, but they do not show it?</div> </div> </div> </div>So is Seeming visible on the Fae-Touched, or only &quot;in their souls&quot;? Fairest are more beautiful than normal people? Beasts are savage and animal-like?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 05-27-2015, 03:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-27T01:41:20-07:00","id":529682,"title":"","content":"Fae-touched seeming seems to be mostly an affinity thing. It's all in their head. <br /> <br /> Also I think it might be difficult to just casually drop a transgender character in without comment like the other two examples. Unambiguously anyway. Theoretically <i>any</i> character referred to in passing could be trans. How would we know?<br /> <br /> Not to mention any werewolf with a dot of Honor renown can learn to flip sex at will.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-27T01:42:24-07:00","id":529683,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/528342-the-fae-touched?p=529668#post529668\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's second best representation of LGBT characters in 2ED corebooks. First is still in <b>Werewolf: The Forsaken </b>Touchstones section, where male cop character truly loves his boyfriend and want's to be his husband, but understand that him being Uratha would put his loved one in to danger if they would be &quot;serious&quot;. We have gay and lesbian relationships - now I wait for transgender people in <b>Mage </b>2ED. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>That one was mine. Thank you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-27T05:19:18-07:00","id":529808,"title":"","content":"Oh, I love them! So much potential for countless stories.<br /> Question-if Wyrd can rise above 0, what is maximum of it? I doubt fae touched can go up to 10.<br /> Also, I agree-great representation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6005-coolcat12345","name":"coolcat12345","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-27T05:32:49-07:00","id":529812,"title":"","content":"If it's anything like how ghouls work (and a lot of their other mechanics seem similar) they'll be stuck at Wyrd 0.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-27T06:31:30-07:00","id":529864,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/528342-the-fae-touched?p=529812#post529812\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If it's anything like how ghouls work (and a lot of their other mechanics seem similar) they'll be stuck at Wyrd 0.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think they'll be stuck at 0. I'm willing to hear thoughts to the contrary before I get there. But I intend for them to work like ghouls.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-27T07:35:05-07:00","id":529933,"title":"","content":"Heh, now I wonder how many Alien Abduction stories are garbled memories of a Fae-Touched's trip into the Hedge","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/209-that-other-guy","name":"That Other Guy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-27T07:54:46-07:00","id":529955,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>That Other Guy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/528342-the-fae-touched?p=529933#post529933\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Heh, now I wonder how many Alien Abduction stories are garbled memories of a Fae-Touched's trip into the Hedge</div> </div> </div> </div>The abduction part makes it seem more like actual Changelings than Fae Touched. There's even a Kith for &quot;alien&quot; abductees. A Fae-Touched goes in after someone, which doesn't line up with the alien abduction narrative. Abductees are taken forcibly, they don't willingly go in search of someone who disappeared.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-27T09:43:13-07:00","id":530066,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/528342-the-fae-touched?p=529864#post529864\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think they'll be stuck at 0. I'm willing to hear thoughts to the contrary before I get there. But I intend for them to work like ghouls.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, there's the <i>easy, if a little suicidal</i> way: get properly abducted by one of the Gentry. The fact that Fae-touched feel a compulsion to reenter the Hedge doesn't preclude the possibility of being changed in that manner, to my thinking. In fact, it's more desirable for the Fae in that most of the creative work is already done.<br /> <br /> FWIW, I felt like the Fae-touched, from this reading, had more in common with Revenants than Ghouls, as far as the limits of their powers were concerned.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-27T12:37:52-07:00","id":530218,"title":"","content":"Unless Wyrd has changed a lot since 1E, I wouldn't mind fae-touched being stuck at Wyrd 1. Low Wyrd doesn't quite have the same status that blood potency does. Ghouls are more inherently subservient to vampires, even blood potency 1 vampires. Since fae-touched can use contracts and glamour anyway (the hallmark of Wyrd) I think Wyrd 1 fits better. It would emphasise that they began the process of becoming a changeling without going all the way. It would also make them more like fetches, assuming fetches still start with Wyrd 1. Its not a big deal either way although just stating they are stuck at Wyrd 1 would perhaps save words instead of explaining what Wyrd 0 actually means in play.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1161-gravitas-man","name":"Gravitas Man","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1161_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-27T13:13:02-07:00","id":530254,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hexmeister Vic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/528342-the-fae-touched?p=530066#post530066\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">FWIW, I felt like the Fae-touched, from this reading, had more in common with Revenants than Ghouls, as far as the limits of their powers were concerned.</div> </div> </div> </div>From a story perspective, yes, but mechanically speaking, they seem much closer to Ghouls to me. Revenants have no Clan and treat all Disciplines as out-of-clan, but can learn Disciplines on their own. Ghouls are considered the same Clan as their Regnant and pay in-Clan costs for their Clan Disciplines, but must be taught by a vampire. Fae-Touched are considered the same Seeming as the Changeling who helped them escape, start with two dots of their Seeming's Contracts, and can learn their Seeming's Contract Bonuses but must be taught by a changeling. Revenants have BP1, can only hold 5 + Stamina Vitae, and lose all Vitae when they awaken. Ghouls have BP 0, can hold Stamina Vitae, don't lose it except through normal use, and can't feed from mortals, but can be given Vitae by their Regnant. Fae-Touched in this draft have Wyrd 0, can hold 10 Glamour, don't lose it except through normal use, and can't harvest it from dreams, but can harvest it from emotions or Hedge Bounty.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gravitas Man</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/528342-the-fae-touched?p=530218#post530218\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Unless Wyrd has changed a lot since 1E, I wouldn't mind fae-touched being stuck at Wyrd 1. Low Wyrd doesn't quite have the same status that blood potency does. Ghouls are more inherently subservient to vampires, even blood potency 1 vampires. Since fae-touched can use contracts and glamour anyway (the hallmark of Wyrd) I think Wyrd 1 fits better. It would emphasise that they began the process of becoming a changeling without going all the way. It would also make them more like fetches, assuming fetches still start with Wyrd 1. Its not a big deal either way although just stating they are stuck at Wyrd 1 would perhaps save words instead of explaining what Wyrd 0 actually means in play.</div> </div> </div> </div>It didn't take much space to explain what BP 0 meant in vampire. Just one line on the Blood Potency chart and the Sun Damage chart. I imagine Wyrd 0 would be similar.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-27T13:22:36-07:00","id":530259,"title":"","content":"If memory serves, the glamour used to Ensorcel some mortals can make them more prone to insanity (I believe this is discussed in Autumn Nightmares). If its necessary to have a major drawback for Fae-Touched, maybe the touch of Glamour makes them more vulnerable to losing their still human minds instead of shortening their lifespans?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2244-nothri","name":"nothri","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"485"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-27T13:33:19-07:00","id":530264,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nothri</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/528342-the-fae-touched?p=530259#post530259\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If memory serves, the glamour used to Ensorcel some mortals can make them more prone to insanity (I believe this is discussed in Autumn Nightmares). If its necessary to have a major drawback for Fae-Touched, maybe the touch of Glamour makes them more vulnerable to losing their still human minds instead of shortening their lifespans?</div> </div> </div> </div>Susceptible to Madness is already a drawback of the fae-touched in the draft and it dovetails with Hedge Addiction in mechanical incentives.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-27T13:33:56-07:00","id":530267,"title":"","content":"On the Fae Touched themselves, I have mixed feelings. On the one hand I think Changeling has needed something akin to this for awhile. On the other, the origin of the Fae Touched seems a little...specific. Don't get me wrong, I like the idea that the Lost can have such an intimate tie to their version of the Ghoul (for lack of a better term). At the same time, when I consider all the ways the Wyrd can touch the lives of humanity it feels wrong that Fae-Touched only come about in these rather particular circumstances. I wonder if there aren't other, Fae-Touched like humans out there, exposed to the Wyrd in a somewhat different way with a similar outcome (similar to how sometimes a mortal can apparently be Ensorceled without ever making a Pledge). <br /> <br /> Then too, there's the question of what happens to a Fae-Touched who's Changeling can't muster the memory to leave Arcadia? Do they still develop a Seeming? Since the majority of Changelings never make it back, that potentially means that the Fae-Touched outnumber the changelings, right? What happens to a Fae-Touched if their Changeling exceeds their Wyrd and becomes a True Fae? On that note, can the True Fae manifest their own Fae-Touched?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2244-nothri","name":"nothri","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"485"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-27T13:43:27-07:00","id":530275,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nothri</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/528342-the-fae-touched?p=530267#post530267\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the Fae Touched themselves, I have mixed feelings. On the one hand I think Changeling has needed something akin to this for awhile. On the other, the origin of the Fae Touched seems a little...specific. Don't get me wrong, I like the idea that the Lost can have such an intimate tie to their version of the Ghoul (for lack of a better term). At the same time, when I consider all the ways the Wyrd can touch the lives of humanity it feels wrong that Fae-Touched only come about in these rather particular circumstances. I wonder if there aren't other, Fae-Touched like humans out there, exposed to the Wyrd in a somewhat different way with a similar outcome (similar to how sometimes a mortal can apparently be Ensorceled without ever making a Pledge).<br /> <br /> Then too, there's the question of what happens to a Fae-Touched who's Changeling can't muster the memory to leave Arcadia? Do they still develop a Seeming? Since the majority of Changelings never make it back, that potentially means that the Fae-Touched outnumber the changelings, right? What happens to a Fae-Touched if their Changeling exceeds their Wyrd and becomes a True Fae? On that note, can the True Fae manifest their own Fae-Touched?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Changeling doesn't have to make it back with the Fae-Touched. In fact, the draft makes it sound to me like the vast majority of Fae-Touched never find their Changeling, and either wander out of the Hedge or are lead out by some other Changeling that happens upon them. The implication to me is that Fae-Touched are <i>extremely </i>rare. So many things have to fall into place for one to be created and make it back out again.Not that many people are taken to Arcadia in the first place<br /> <br /> Of those few who are taken, not all of them are likely to have people who made such a deep, significant promise to them<br /> Of those who do, not all of them will go looking for the missing promisee<br /> Of those who do, not all of them will ever make it into the Hedge<br /> Of those who do, not all of them will ever make it back out again<br /> <br /> So it seems to me like Fae-Touched are outliers of a set of outliers of a set of outliers. That does make them fairly specific, yes, but when you look at stories about these kinds of characters - again, Labyrinth is a good example of a story that focuses on such a character - that seems fairly appropriate, don't you think?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-27T14:05:51-07:00","id":530301,"title":"","content":"And yet they have their own subsociety adjacent to the freehold; I think exactly how common they are needs to be addressed directly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-27T14:24:13-07:00","id":530315,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/528342-the-fae-touched?p=530301#post530301\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And yet they have their own subsociety adjacent to the freehold; I think exactly how common they are needs to be addressed directly.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm pretty sure it is - the Wyrd draws them to each other.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-27T16:28:17-07:00","id":530392,"title":"","content":"The logistics of how common fae-touched are in a freehold is!<br /> <br /> However common or uncommon you want them for your story.<br /> <br /> Huh. Well that was easy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 05-27-2015, 09:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-27T16:35:38-07:00","id":530395,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/528342-the-fae-touched?p=530275#post530275\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not that many people are taken to Arcadia in the first place</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree with the point that Fae-Touched are rare (although, defining &quot;rare&quot; in terms of a supernatural population that only exists as a fraction of a percent of the human population to begin with is a whole other issue), but do we actually know this? At least, in terms of those Changelings who escape? Going by 1E, Fae are bound to give their victims an opportunity to get the heck out of dodge, but they don't by any means need to make it easy. I've heard people speculate that for every Changeling who gets out, there could be ten or more left behind in Arcadia. It doesn't sound entirely unreasonable, given how much the Fae <i>need</i> their victims.<br /> <br /> And from that point, the Fae-Touched start to diverge dramatically from the Changelings in a Freehold. If you were to construct a Venn Diagram of Fae-Touched and Changelings who escaped together, it would necessarily be small for all the reasons you described. But while becoming a Fae-Touched is unlikely, becoming a Changeling (at least, a post-Arcadia escapee) requires a Changeling to go through almost everything a Fae-Touched has to go through.<br /> <br /> Finally, yeah, not all people who are taken are going to have others who have made deep, meaningful promises to them. But I wouldn't say that those who have are going to be &quot;outliers&quot;. We humans are social beings, I would say the overwhelming majority of us rely on others in a whole range of different ways. Close ties to other human beings, to family and close friends and significant others, are kind of the norm aren't they? Narratively, yeah, we tend to depict them as something special, and they are certainly something special for those involved, but they're not <i>unique</i> by any stretch of the imagination.<br /> <br /> I guess what I'm kind of grappling with here is that for every question you ask, I could ask a similar one about a Changeling. We kind of accept the existence of Changelings as the norm, the default that exists so that the Chronicle may happen, but see:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/528342-the-fae-touched?p=530275#post530275\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Of those who do, not all of them will go looking for the missing promise</div> </div> </div> </div>Of those who are taken to Arcadia, how many will actually try to escape?<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/528342-the-fae-touched?p=530275#post530275\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Of those who do, not all of them will ever make it into the Hedge</div> </div> </div> </div>Of those Changelings who do try, how many will ever make it out of Arcadia and into the Hedge?<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/528342-the-fae-touched?p=530275#post530275\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Of those who do, not all of them will ever make it back out again</div> </div> </div> </div>The Hedge is dangerous. The same goes for Changelings.<br /> <br /> So yes, absolutely, Fae-Touched are rare as all heck. But so are Changelings. Freeholds may not be aware of the existence of all the Fae-Touched in their area, but Fae-Touched could easily rival the Changeling population in raw numbers. Probably a little smaller than a 1-to-1 ratio on account of those that would avoid Changelings or never encounter them after becoming Fae-Touched, but still a comparable number.<br /> <br /> Of course, the added caveat that &quot;there are as many as you want for a Chronicle&quot; goes double in a world where the Wyrd exists, but rationally I see each as likely as the other.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1059,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","user":"Azahul","date":". 05-27-2015, 07:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-27T19:57:42-07:00","id":530562,"title":"","content":"Excellent points all, Azahul. That would certainly make it seem as though their populations would be fairly close in number (unless the story demands otherwise, obviously).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-27T21:51:18-07:00","id":530654,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/528342-the-fae-touched?p=529668#post529668\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> We have gay and lesbian relationships - now I wait for transgender people in <b>Mage </b>2ED. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>We've had a transwoman already in Demon: The Descent, which seems to be a trend for the 2nd ed game lines. Improved flavor, improved mechanics, improved representation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://blood-and-bourbon.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Blood and Bourbon</a>, my New Orleans-based Vampire chronicle.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3110-false-epiphany","name":"False Epiphany","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3110_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"748"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-27T22:02:28-07:00","id":530670,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>False Epiphany</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/528342-the-fae-touched?p=530654#post530654\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> We've had a transwoman already in Demon: The Descent, which seems to be a trend for the 2nd ed game lines. Improved flavor, improved mechanics, improved representation.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's one in Mummy's Cursed Necropolis D.C. as well, and the sample Mummy in Mortal Remains too.<br /> <br /> That said, the way this particular bit of representation was included was exceedingly elegant. I approve.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1059,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","user":"Azahul","date":". 05-28-2015, 01:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-28T10:26:52-07:00","id":531116,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Azahul</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/528342-the-fae-touched?p=530670#post530670\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">and the sample Mummy in Mortal Remains too.</div> </div> </div> </div>They should have made that sample Mummy an Agis Kai Doru agent instead. No cult, no long history, a distinctly modern gender identity.<br /> <br /> (Now a Mummy charachter based on Ancient Egyptian ideas of transgenderism would be an awesome sample charachter. Though I think those ideas have been lost to history)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 05-28-2015, 01:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-28T10:36:47-07:00","id":531123,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>False Epiphany</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/528342-the-fae-touched?p=530654#post530654\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> We've had a transwoman already in Demon: The Descent, which seems to be a trend for the 2nd ed game lines. Improved flavor, improved mechanics, improved representation.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also, the crowning achievement of Onyx Path's representation, Luna's Embrace in Werewolf 2nd.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-28T11:15:37-07:00","id":531154,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/528342-the-fae-touched?p=531123#post531123\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, the crowning achievement of Onyx Path's representation, Luna's Embrace in Werewolf 2nd.</div> </div> </div> </div> Is Luna's Embrace more than just a sex swap power? (My info is just google)<br /> <br /> I'm just a little suprised to hear it called the crowning achievement when that was possible with Life Arcana way back in Mage Core.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-28T11:18:53-07:00","id":531158,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/528342-the-fae-touched?p=531154#post531154\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Is Luna's Embrace more than just a sex swap power? (My info is just google)<br /> <br /> I'm just a little suprised to hear it called the crowning achievement when that was possible with Life Arcana way back in Mage Core.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that occured to me minutes after I posted. I was, and still am, sleep drunk.<br /> <br /> But I found it awesome either way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-28T12:27:54-07:00","id":531202,"title":"","content":"Although Luna's Embrace is written in binary terms, missing an opportunity for intersex representation. I still love the power, but it could have been even better.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-28T13:02:45-07:00","id":531217,"title":"","content":"That's a 3-dot fetish waiting to happen.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-28T17:27:33-07:00","id":531409,"title":"","content":"I have an idea for a fae-touched; but it doesn't really benefit from trying to assign Contracts to it \u2014 I'm basing her loosely off of Karin Murphy from the Dresden Files, with <i>just enough</i> in the way of supernatural chops to be able to enter and exit the Hedge and to interact with changelings and fetches without their Masks getting in the way. Would it be reasonable to replace one or both of the Contracts that the fae-touched are assigned with Fae-Touched (or other) merits, such as taking a Promise of Love without having to devote two Merit dots to it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-28T17:46:13-07:00","id":531433,"title":"","content":"I place money on them being about the same EXP cost, sooooooo probably?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-28T19:56:48-07:00","id":531577,"title":"","content":"Also, I'm a little bothered by the bit about \u201cas soon as she enters the Hedge, she becomes fae-touched\u201d. Granted, becoming fae-touched only happens to someone who has made a promise to someone who has been abducted by the fae; so not just <i>anyone</i> who enters the hedge becomes fae-touched. But I'd be more comfortable if there was some period of adjustment, where if you get out \u201csoon enough\u201d, you remain a mostly-ordinary mortal (i.e., no Wyrd, no Seeming, no Contracts) who maybe picks up a Supernatural Merit such as Unseen Sense or Enchanted Mortal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-31T05:37:54-07:00","id":534229,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/528342-the-fae-touched?p=531577#post531577\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, I'm a little bothered by the bit about \u201cas soon as she enters the Hedge, she becomes fae-touched\u201d. Granted, becoming fae-touched only happens to someone who has made a promise to someone who has been abducted by the fae; so not just <i>anyone</i> who enters the hedge becomes fae-touched. But I'd be more comfortable if there was some period of adjustment, where if you get out \u201csoon enough\u201d, you remain a mostly-ordinary mortal (i.e., no Wyrd, no Seeming, no Contracts) who maybe picks up a Supernatural Merit such as Unseen Sense or Enchanted Mortal.</div> </div> </div> </div>You could always do the similar sorts of things they did for Demon-blooded in Heirs to Hell and have advancing conditions - the lowest level was functionally invisible (but encouraged eventual lapse) unless you invited it along in the narrative.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1462-xenesis","name":"Xenesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1462_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-01T06:12:16-07:00","id":535504,"title":"","content":"It's a a Wolf Gift. Moon gifts are the ones only a specific auspice can learn. Wolf gifts are the ones everyone has as affinity by default.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-01T07:53:35-07:00","id":535580,"title":"","content":"Well, then! A new human-splat for the changelings! Its certainly exciting to see the Lost join the ranks of the ghoul, new wolfblood, and sleepwalkers/proximi. It is certainly interesting!<br /> <br /> <br /> <i><u><b>The Good</b></u></i><br /> Oh, my, where to start? I love the idea of the mortal+ splat being drawn by a promise to rescue their beloved friend/family/significant other. It feels like the fae touched are kind of like Search and Rescue people to the changeling's being Lost. Which is just wonderful balance. I can see a lot of potential there. I must admit, I do like the idea of being fundamentally bonded to one of the fae people, much like the ghouls are bound to a specific vampire, and it would be interesting to see how the Courts play out that bond. Especially if the one we're bound to goes bad. I must say that the mortal+ have been some of my favorite material in 2e, and Lost's version does not disappoint on that matter!<br /> <br /> While the origin of the FT is pretty strict, what the actual touched can be like, do, or act is wonderfully detailed in great lengths. Court, outcast, and loyalist FT are rather nice touches. The loyalist touched actually have left me with a good idea for a plot going forwards that I'm interested in running as soon as the book comes out! <br /> <br /> Abilities - giving them some pledge crafting is rather curious. Now, we haven't seen what we can do, but I do find the ability to pledge only the fae to be rather curious, making the unwary fae fall into a word trap. Can't really talk more about this without more information about the different kinds of pledges, we seem to be involved with. I can't really comment on the whole Contract bit, though I would like to say that I like the idea of being restricted to Seeming-only ones. The EXP tax, though, seems unnecessary <br /> <br /> Hedge addiction and Madness - amusing in a &quot;down the rabbit hole&quot; way, keep going back. Though, I think it should be in the form of new Conditions, if not the standard addiction Conditions we already have. Its curious, how we crave the rush of being inflicted with Madness. I keep going back to Alice, who keeps going down the rabbit hole, only to come back Mad as a Hatter. Or maybe the Hatter she met was a touched with Madness. <br /> <br /> Merits - with the exception of dream (see below), I do like the merits, a lot which emphases the role as promise keepers. The &quot;Promised To&quot; line is especially interesting, as it is a kind of reinforcement of fae-touched-seemings, imho. I liked it in vamp and wolf when the did it as well. <br /> <br /> <b><u><i>The Bad</i></u></b><br /> I join the ranks of those who feel that the fae touched are portrayed as exceedingly rare and difficult to arrange. Now, I know that the actual rarity is up to the ST to decide, but I think that the portrayal, as written, is going to influence readers in a way that's less than desirable. Not only are we talking about 1) a promise of some kind, 2) realize the fetch isn't real person, and 3) stumbling into the Hedge, but also 4) finding the way out, 5) surviving hostile terrain, and possibly 6) finding a changeling to teach them. Its a very specific set of circumstances that likely requires some amount of skill. So, I'd almost like to see all of them have some guide for that initial entering of the Hedge, and perhaps something supernatural to guide them towards the changeling, and perhaps away from danger, and back home. This is touched upon in the Drawback section, but it really should have something in the advantage section too. Speaking of the Arcadian Dreams... the penalty should really come in the form of a Condition.<br /> <br /> The relationship between changelings and fae touched seems a bit odd. In one part, it talks about how most changelings keep fae touched at a distance, then the very next paragraph, we're talking about how relationships are widely varied. Later on, under Oath Keepers, it talks about how they hope to be reunited with their others, but both earlier and later we're talking about how the fae touched entering the Hedge helps trigger an escape, and can meet up with the changeling. I feel that we're getting too many mixed messages here - a bit of clarification would be lovely on the bond between changeling and touched. Its such a central part of the character that I think it needs to be explored more.<br /> <br /> I have to ask why keeping <i>all </i>promises is important to the fae touched - there are plenty of people that will only keep their words to close friends and family, and have no qualms about breaking any other promise. Or maybe only a promise sworn under certain circumstances. Why so restrictive? What's so markedly different than standard pledging? It feels like they're trying to be more truthful than the changelings are required to be! Especially when they can only pledge with fae.<br /> <br /> Short Lifespan - just... yeah. Moving on.<br /> <br /> Hedge Addiction and Madness - while the addiction to the hedge was nicely covered, there's a notable lack of the madness that fae touched will suffer from when they return from the Hedge. I think we should really have some word count devoted to that.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure how I feel about the glamour pool being so high, and the lack of ability to use catches. My knee jerk reaction is that it should actually be reversed, activating Contracts only through catches (thanks to activating tokens via catches in the past). Now, unless catches are vastly different than 1e, the explanation doesn't make sense to me - catches are just certain actions you take, which are very easy to teach. Especially when they can form pledges and balance those out. I'm guessing its a thematic thing, where we don't want the touched to act and dress like the fae, or something to that effect? I'm not sure on it. I don't know if its bad, but I'd like to test it out, or hear some idea why its this way.<br /> <br /> Merits - Dream merits are way too expensive for something that you basically need changeling help to do in the first place. Its a lot of investment for something that may not come up. In my experience, the dreams tend to be less important unless necessary for plot, at which point, we're looking at a tax to join a story. Not a fan. <br /> <br /> Fae Mein - makes no sense from what we know of Seemings and the like. No reason to restrict Contracts based on having a mein or not - its arbitrarily restrictive.<br /> <br /> <b><u><i>The Ugly</i></u></b><br /> Pedro. Naught, naughty boy for leaving his beloved friend to rot so long in the Hedge without telling anyone. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-01T11:50:41-07:00","id":535758,"title":"","content":"You know, I watched the Poltergeist remake yesterday, and Griffin makes for a pretty good example of a fae-touched, I think, braving the perilous otherworld to rescue his ghost-kidnapped sister Maddy. Also the idea of a particularly disturbing part of the Hedge where the thorns take the form of a wall of grasping corpse-hands is definitely a thing that will be incorporated into the next game of Changeling I run.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-01T13:36:27-07:00","id":535902,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/528342-the-fae-touched?p=535580#post535580\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hedge addiction and Madness - amusing in a &quot;down the rabbit hole&quot; way, keep going back. Though, I think it should be in the form of new Conditions, if not the standard addiction Conditions we already have.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Speaking of the Arcadian Dreams... the penalty should really come in the form of a Condition. </div> </div> </div>I agree with this. I don't see why Hedge Addiction can't be represented by Addiction and Deprivation, with a guideline for how often a Fae-Touched needs to get their fix.<br /> <br /> Also, it seems a little harsh that they can take penalties to rolls after entering the hedge (until they resolve Madness, which isn't an easy one to resolve) and then they take additional penalties once per story due to Arcadian Dreams. That's a lot of penalties to be taking. Perhaps Arcadian Dreams should be represented by an Obsession condition that can only be purged when the Changeling they're connected with is out of Arcadia. And maybe, since it's pretty difficult to resolve, Susceptible to Madness should be once a story like Arcadian Dreams is currently, except just when entering the hedge.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5910-csschulz","name":"CSSchulz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5910_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-01T14:14:33-07:00","id":535918,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CSSchulz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/528342-the-fae-touched?p=535902#post535902\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, it seems a little harsh that they can take penalties to rolls after entering the hedge (until they resolve Madness, which isn't an easy one to resolve) and then they take additional penalties once per story due to Arcadian Dreams. That's a lot of penalties to be taking. Perhaps Arcadian Dreams should be represented by an Obsession condition that can only be purged when the Changeling they're connected with is out of Arcadia. And maybe, since it's pretty difficult to resolve, Susceptible to Madness should be once a story like Arcadian Dreams is currently, except just when entering the hedge.</div> </div> </div> </div>Note that it is <i>much easier</i> for a Fae-Touched to resolve Madness than it is for a normal mortal, thanks to their Seeming Blessing which gives them a free way to gain a dot of Integrity once per story. If they could only gain the Madness once per story, it would be a minor inconvenience at best to resolve.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-01T14:29:13-07:00","id":535942,"title":"","content":"I found a problem, part of the Beast's Seeming curse refers to an innate power that Changelings have, but Fae-Touched do not. It casts beasts three glamour to free themselves from restraints instead of the usual 1 glamour as part of they're curse, which works fine for Changelings, but Fae-Touched don't have the ability to free themselves from restraints. I see three solutions, 1. make it clear that only the parts of a Seemings blessings and curses that make sense for a Faetouched go into effect for Fae-Touched, 2. Gives Fae-Touched the ability to free themselves from restraints, this would not be over powered so its my preperence 3. Change the Beast Seeming.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-01T15:04:40-07:00","id":535981,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/528342-the-fae-touched?p=535918#post535918\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Note that it is <i>much easier</i> for a Fae-Touched to resolve Madness than it is for a normal mortal, thanks to their Seeming Blessing which gives them a free way to gain a dot of Integrity once per story. If they could only gain the Madness once per story, it would be a minor inconvenience at best to resolve.</div> </div> </div> </div>Good point. Hadn't considered that. I guess their Seeming Curse might cause them to resolve it, too. I still maintain that Conditions would be best for Hedge Addiction (Addiction and Deprivation - like with Ghouls and Vitae) and Arcadian Dreams (Obsession).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5910-csschulz","name":"CSSchulz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5910_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-01T15:23:32-07:00","id":535994,"title":"","content":"I agree. Using Conditions is always better than free-floating mechanics.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-01T17:23:03-07:00","id":536268,"title":"","content":"Is it possible that the Seemings of the fae-touched have <i>no effects</i> beyond what they do to Contracts? e.g., since they don't have Clarity, they don't get the Clarity Breaking Points embedded in the Curses? Seeming would still be useful due to its impact on the Contracts; but it wouldn't have nearly as much of an impact on the Fae-Touched as it has on changelings. Which seems appropriate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-01T17:35:56-07:00","id":536275,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/528342-the-fae-touched?p=536268#post536268\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is it possible that the Seemings of the fae-touched have <i>no effects</i> beyond what they do to Contracts? e.g., since they don't have Clarity, they don't get the Clarity Breaking Points embedded in the Curses? Seeming would still be useful due to its impact on the Contracts; but it wouldn't have nearly as much of an impact on the Fae-Touched as it has on changelings. Which seems appropriate.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh. I'm favoring Integrity. It's a little touch of tragedy in there; you don't have Clarity and its inherent benefits, but you're a little more fragile. On the other hand, you also have something that empowers you if you run with it. So, some grace, too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-01T18:35:36-07:00","id":536324,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/528342-the-fae-touched?p=536275#post536275\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Eh. I'm favoring Integrity. It's a little touch of tragedy in there; you don't have Clarity and its inherent benefits, but you're a little more fragile. On the other hand, you also have something that empowers you if you run with it. So, some grace, too.</div> </div> </div> </div>By &quot;inherent benefits&quot;, you mean Kenning, right?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-01T18:46:26-07:00","id":536357,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/528342-the-fae-touched?p=536324#post536324\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> By &quot;inherent benefits&quot;, you mean Kenning, right?</div> </div> </div> </div>Probably specific points of breaking as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-01T19:10:36-07:00","id":536379,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/528342-the-fae-touched?p=536324#post536324\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> By &quot;inherent benefits&quot;, you mean Kenning, right?</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh. That's one of them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-01T19:57:26-07:00","id":536406,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/528342-the-fae-touched?p=536275#post536275\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Eh. I'm favoring Integrity. It's a little touch of tragedy in there; you don't have Clarity and its inherent benefits, but you're a little more fragile. On the other hand, you also have something that empowers you if you run with it. So, some grace, too.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Does that mean that the Fae-Touched's Seeming Blessing and Curse won't apply, or that the Blessing and Curse will affect Integrity instead?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5910-csschulz","name":"CSSchulz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5910_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-01T21:26:37-07:00","id":536473,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CSSchulz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/528342-the-fae-touched?p=536406#post536406\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does that mean that the Fae-Touched's Seeming Blessing and Curse won't apply, or that the Blessing and Curse will affect Integrity instead?</div> </div> </div> </div>We discussed this back on page 2.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/528342-the-fae-touched?p=528577#post528577\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/528342-the-fae-touched?p=528569#post528569\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I noticed Fae-Touched have a Seeming and all its associated benefits (and drawbacks) but they do not have Clarity. I assume that means their Blessing increases their Integrity and their Curse is an Integrity Breaking Point, but the text doesn't specify that and it probably should.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's because it was written before we settled on Seeming Blessings and Curses. I'll note it. I'm pretty sure I'm going with Integrity as the analogue, as noted.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-01T22:42:31-07:00","id":536543,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/528342-the-fae-touched?p=536473#post536473\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We discussed this back on page 2.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Woops! Forgot about that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5910-csschulz","name":"CSSchulz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5910_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-02T22:19:50-07:00","id":537756,"title":"","content":"Looking over it I see we've learned some things about Changeling template as well. One in reguards to dreams, the 2e Changeling template is more powerful, a Changeling can enter dreams by just touching someone, it does not appear the an pledge is needed anymore, and Changelings can now enter dreams physically, via the hedge, and then entering someones Bastion, whatever that is (very curious). Just guessing, but I'm betting that has both advantages and disadvantages.<br /> <br /> Pledges seem to come in three flavours, Sealings, Oaths, and Bargains. Fae seem to be able to act as third parties for sealings, which seals a promise. Oaths I think might be more traditional pledges not sure. Bargains have something called coverage. Very interesting. The only one the Fae Touched seems to be able to do on her own is Sealings, with limits, which suggests its the weakest.<br /> <br /> Just a guess but I think Sealings are just promises that the wyrd punishes if violated some how, but do not grants benifits like merits or skills. Given a Fae Touched can seal them, but Fae Touched have 0 wyrd, I suspect that thier is no limit on how many sealings one can have, and that they're efeect is weaker.<br /> <br /> Oaths are likely more traditional pledges more or less, again just a guess. Parties invovled promise to do x in exchange for Y benifits. I think Fae Touched can.particapate in Oaths, but can't make them.<br /> <br /> Bargains my gut tells me are more powerful and might be more directed at deals between Changelings and None Changeling. I have a feeling they're less about 2 way service then Oaths. Like maybe they're more about trading something in exchange something, instead of a promise to.do action x, your selling like say your soul or beauty or whatever in exchange for something. Just a guess.<br /> <br /> .Question becames where do Pledge Token and Goblin vow fit in to this? Bargains perhaps?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-19T17:57:40-07:00","id":561412,"title":"","content":"Just wanted to let y'all know I have a sheet for 2nd ed Fae-Touch up on the site!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/pdf/CtL/CtL_2ndED_Fae-Touched_1-Page_Editable.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/pdf/CtL/CtL_2ndED_Fae-Touched_1-Page_Editable.pdf\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/pdf/CtL/CtL_2ndED_Fae-Touched_1-Page_Editable.pdf\" target=\"_blank\"> http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/pdf/CtL/CtL_2ndED_Fae-Touched_1-Page_Editable.pdf </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> wyrdhamster requested it and helped with the info. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _______________________